    "name": "introduction",
    "title": "Survey Introduction",
    "elements": [],
    "description": "Welcome to the Urban Streetscape Bikeability Survey. This research examines the effectiveness of design interventions and socio-economic impacts on bikeability across various urban contexts. \n\n**Research Question:** How do design interventions and socio-economic factors influence the bikeability of urban environments?"
   },
   {
    "name": "methodology",
    "title": "Methodology and Sampling Strategy",
    "elements": [],
    "description": "This survey targets urban cyclists from diverse backgrounds. We aim to collect responses from 1,000 cyclists using both online and offline methods, such as partnering with local community organizations and conducting paper surveys in key urban areas. This approach ensures a representative sample across different urban contexts."
   },
